<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47684" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tĕmĕnos</span></b> , = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέμενος, τό,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a place at Syracuse
				sacred to Apollo;</i> hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tĕmĕnītes</span></b> ,
			is, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τεμενίτης,</span>
			<i>an epithet of Apollo</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Cic. Verr 2, 4, 53, §
			119</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Suet. Tib. 74</span></i>. —
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tĕmĕnītis</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τεμενῖτις,</span>
			<i>a fountain at Syracuse</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 8,
				14, § 89</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
